  <h2 id="behaviour">Behaviour</h2>
  <p>Charts work as static HTML: tooltips open on hover and keyboard focus with CSS alone. Add <code>data-dd-chart</code> to the <code>.dd-chart</code> figure and the script adds the rest:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>One tab stop per plot.</b> Slots, line points (<code>__hit</code>), 100% segments (<code>__seg</code>) and donut arcs (<code>__arc</code>) — or any element with <code>data-dd-chart-point</code> — share a roving <code>tabindex</code>. <kbd class="dd-kbd">←</kbd> <kbd class="dd-kbd">→</kbd> (or <kbd class="dd-kbd">↑</kbd> <kbd class="dd-kbd">↓</kbd>) step through them, <kbd class="dd-kbd">Home</kbd> / <kbd class="dd-kbd">End</kbd> jump to the ends, <kbd class="dd-kbd">Esc</kbd> hides the tooltip until the next move.</li>
    <li><b>Touch.</b> Tapping a mark opens its tooltip; tapping anywhere else closes it. Tooltips flip to the side with room.</li>
    <li><b>Floating tooltips.</b> Marks without a <code>.dd-chart__tip</code> inside get one built from <code>data-dd-chart-label</code>, <code>data-dd-chart-value</code> and an optional <code>data-dd-chart-title</code>, keyed by the mark’s series class. Give each mark <code>role="img"</code> and an <code>aria-label</code>, and its container <code>role="group"</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Table view.</b> A <code>&lt;details class="dd-chart__data"&gt;</code> “View as table” needs no script. To swap the plot for its table instead, add a toggle button <code>data-dd-chart-view aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="ID"</code> and a <code>.dd-chart__data.dd-chart__data--swap</code> container with that ID and <code>hidden</code>; the figure gets <code>.is-table</code> and fires <code>dd:change</code> with <code>detail.view</code> = <code>"table"</code> or <code>"chart"</code>.</li>
    <li>The active mark has <code>.is-active</code> (same look as hover); use it to style custom marks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
  <Guides
    do={[
      `Pick the form from the job: columns or bars for comparing amounts, lines for change over time, a 100% bar or donut for parts of one whole, a <a href="${docs}/components/stat">stat</a> for a single number.`,
      'Assign series colours in the fixed order and keep each series’ colour when filters change.',
      'Label selectively: the line ends, the extreme, the one series the story is about. Let the axis, tooltip and table carry the rest.',
      'Round ticks to clean numbers and compact large ones on the axis (0 · 10K · 20K).',
      'Give every chart a name (<code>aria-label</code> or caption) and a table view.',
    ]}
    dont={[
      'Don’t use two y axes. Two measures of different scale get two charts.',
      'Don’t colour text with a series colour — the swatch beside it carries identity.',
      'Don’t reuse status colours (ok, warn, bad) as series; they mean state.',
      'Don’t dash gridlines or draw borders around marks; gaps and rings separate them.',
      'Don’t go past four series in one chart — fold the rest into “Other” or use small multiples.',
    ]}
  />
</Docs>
